New evidence
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ergebnisse - Die Bundeswahlleiterin","publisher":"Die Bundeswahlleiterin","publication_date":"2021-10-15","url":"https://www.bundeswahlleiterin.de/bundestagswahlen/2021/ergebnisse.html","claim":"The 2021 Bundestag election was formally certified, with SPD at 25.7 percent of second votes and the new Bundestag at 736 seats; the page also notes the archived final result for the 26 September 2021 election.","locator":"section 'Ergebnisse bei der Hauptwahl vom 26. September 2021' and results table","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary electoral authority source with certified result data.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Inherited baseline immediately before the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Baseline context, not direct Scholz conduct; it establishes the competitive election that brought him to office.","contrary_evidence":["This is a 2021 baseline, not 2022 conduct.","It shows the system, not any ruler-specific democratic reform."],"lenses":["4B.1","4B.8"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Einsprüche anlässlich der Wahl zum 20. Deutschen Bundestag","publisher":"Deutscher Bundestag","publication_date":"2022-11-10","url":"https://www.bundestag.de/parlament/plenum/abstimmung/abstimmung/?id=816","claim":"The Bundestag voted on the Wahlprüfungsausschuss recommendation for election objections concerning the 2021 federal election; the page explains that election review is a Bundestag matter and that any eligible voter can file an objection and later appeal to the Constitutional Court.","locator":"section 'Der Wahlprüfungsausschuss' and the vote result block","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary parliamentary record of lawful post-election review and legislative processing.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and directly relevant to electoral contestability.","ruler_attribution":"Institutional rather than personal; it reflects the democratic review architecture under Scholz's chancellorship.","contrary_evidence":["This is review after the prior election, not evidence of a 2022 contested election campaign.","The decision path runs through parliament rather than the executive."],"lenses":["4B.1","4B.4","4B.8"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Urteil vom 22. März 2022","publisher":"Bundesverfassungsgericht","publication_date":"2022-03-22","url":"https://www.bundesverfassungsgericht.de/SharedDocs/Entscheidungen/DE/2022/03/es20220322_2bve000920.html","claim":"The Court said the Basic Law does not create specific opposition-franchise rights, but it recognizes effective opposition as a constitutional principle and held the applicant was not obviously violated by the election of Bundestag vice presidents.","locator":"paras. 41-42","source_type":"primary/legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Authoritative constitutional ruling on parliamentary opposition rights and free mandate.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 institutional-oversight evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Institutional, not personal; it shows judicially enforced democratic constraints during Scholz's term.","contrary_evidence":["The court also declined to invent stronger opposition-specific rights.","It confirms that some opposition grievances can fail within a still-democratic framework."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.4","4B.8"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Gericht lehnt AfD-Eilantrag zur Ausschussvorsitzendenwahl ab","publisher":"Deutscher Bundestag","publication_date":"2022-06-23","url":"https://www.bundestag.de/dokumente/textarchiv/2022/kw25-bvg-entscheidung-900080","claim":"The Bundestag reported that the Constitutional Court rejected the AfD's request to install its committee-chair nominees and explained that the committees had used a free majority vote to choose their chairs.","locator":"opening summary and section 'AfD-Kandidaten nicht zu Ausschussvorsitzenden gewählt'","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official parliamentary report on a contemporaneous court decision affecting opposition office access.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 check on parliamentary competition and minority rights.","ruler_attribution":"Institutional rather than Scholz-personal; it reflects parliamentary autonomy under his government.","contrary_evidence":["The majority could deny opposition nominees those posts.","That is a democratic contest mechanism, not evidence of entrenchment."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.4","4B.8"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Versammlungsrechtlicher Schutz eines Protestcamps und seiner infrastrukturellen Einrichtungen","publisher":"Bundesverwaltungsgericht","publication_date":"2022-05-24","url":"https://www.bverwg.de/240522U6C9.20.0","claim":"The Federal Administrative Court held that a protest camp can generally be protected as an assembly under Article 8 of the Basic Law and that necessary infrastructure can also fall under assembly protection.","locator":"Leitsätze 1-3","source_type":"primary/legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary domestic judicial ruling on assembly and protest protection.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 rule-of-law evidence on protest space.","ruler_attribution":"Institutional, not personal; the ruling reflects the legal environment during Scholz's chancellorship.","contrary_evidence":["Authorities can still impose limits in some circumstances.","The decision concerns protest rights generally, not Scholz's personal behavior."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.6","4B.9"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Beschluss vom 30. März 2022","publisher":"Bundesverfassungsgericht","publication_date":"2022-03-30","url":"https://www.bundesverfassungsgericht.de/SharedDocs/Entscheidungen/DE/2022/03/rk20220330_1bvr282116.html","claim":"The Court reiterated that press and broadcasting freedom protect the whole journalistic process, including access to needed information and sources, and that the state may not impose indirect pressures that amount to interference.","locator":"paras. 17-18","source_type":"primary/legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Authoritative constitutional decision on media freedom and access to information.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 legal context for media freedom.","ruler_attribution":"Institutional, not personal; it establishes the constitutional framework under Scholz's government.","contrary_evidence":["This does not show a specific Scholz initiative.","It is a general rights ruling rather than a case about media policy."],"lenses":["4B.6","4B.9"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Erfolgreiche Verfassungsbeschwerde gegen die Übermittlung mit nachrichtendienstlichen Mitteln erhobener personenbezogener Daten","publisher":"Bundesverfassungsgericht","publication_date":"2022-11-03","url":"https://www.bundesverfassungsgericht.de/SharedDocs/Pressemitteilungen/DE/2022/bvg22-085.html","claim":"The Court held that statutory rules requiring the transmission of personal data obtained by intelligence methods violated constitutional requirements of legal clarity and proportionality.","locator":"press release body and opening paragraphs","source_type":"primary/legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary constitutional review of surveillance-data transfer limits.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 evidence on surveillance constraints.","ruler_attribution":"Institutional, not personal; it shows judicial limits on surveillance under Scholz.","contrary_evidence":["This is a legal limit, not an executive anti-surveillance initiative.","It does not demonstrate whether the government changed practice immediately."],"lenses":["4B.4","4B.9"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Unterlassene Auskunft der Bundesregierung zur Zahl der im Ausland tätigen Verfassungsschutzbediensteten verletzt parlamentarisches Fragerecht","publisher":"Bundesverfassungsgericht","publication_date":"2022-12-14","url":"https://www.bundesverfassungsgericht.de/SharedDocs/Pressemitteilungen/DE/2022/bvg22-107.html","claim":"The Court ruled that the federal government's refusal to disclose the number of foreign-deployed constitutional-protection employees violated an MP's parliamentary question right.","locator":"press release opening paragraphs","source_type":"primary/legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary ruling on parliamentary oversight and executive disclosure duties.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 oversight evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Institutional rather than personal; it reflects the strength of parliamentary oversight during Scholz's term.","contrary_evidence":["The case concerns disclosure, not direct policy substance.","It shows a check on the executive, not an affirmative freedom-expansion program."],"lenses":["4B.4","4B.8","4B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bundeskabinett - Ergebnisse","publisher":"Bundesregierung","publication_date":"2022-12-14","url":"https://www.bundesregierung.de/breg-de/aktuelles/bundeskabinett-ergebnisse-2153466","claim":"The cabinet adopted a draft law to strengthen democratic participation, diversity, extremism prevention, and political education.","locator":"top section listing agenda items for the 44th cabinet meeting","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous official cabinet decision with clear policy content.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 executive action.","ruler_attribution":"Cabinet-level action under Scholz; it reflects government policy rather than a personal order.","contrary_evidence":["It is a draft-law step, not proof of downstream effects.","The proposal is preventive and indirect rather than a direct rights guarantee."],"lenses":["4B.4","4B.7","4B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Rede von Bundeskanzler Olaf Scholz bei der Chanukka-Feierstunde in der Heinz-Galinski-Schule am 19. Dezember 2022 in Berlin","publisher":"Bundesregierung","publication_date":"2022-12-19","url":"https://www.bundesregierung.de/breg-de/service/newsletter-und-abos/bulletin/rede-von-bundeskanzler-olaf-scholz-2155122","claim":"Scholz used the Chanukka speech to reaffirm Germany's historical responsibility toward Jewish life and remembrance, linking the fight against antisemitism to the protection of Jewish life in Germany.","locator":"opening paragraphs of the speech","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct Scholz speech in the federal bulletin archive.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 public stance on minority equality and protection.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Scholz rhetoric; this is public stance rather than operational policy.","contrary_evidence":["Symbolic speech is not the same as enforcement or institutional reform.","It does not by itself show how anti-antisemitism policy was implemented."],"lenses":["4B.7","4B.10"]}

Search and rejection summary
- I reviewed roughly 25-40 documents across the Federal Government archive, Bundestag, Bundeswahlleiterin, Bundesverfassungsgericht, Bundesverwaltungsgericht, and a smaller set of related press/reporting pages.
- Kept the strongest non-duplicative evidence on election contestability, parliamentary oversight, opposition rights, protest protection, press freedom, surveillance limits, and minority-protection rhetoric/policy.
- Rejected broad democracy-index pages because the local structured priors already cover the regime baseline and re-fetching those datasets was not needed.
- Rejected most media stories about generic politics or coalition disputes because they were either redundant with official constitutional sources or too weakly tied to political-freedom mechanisms.
- Rejected security/Ukraine items unless they had a direct political-freedom effect, since Chapter 4B is about contestability, institutional restraint, and civic/media space rather than international conduct.
- Rejected later 2023-2026 pages when they only restated the same 2022 institutional environment without adding target-period value.
- Rejected incident-heavy or regional items that did not clearly show federal-ruler attribution or did not materially change the chapter picture.

Remaining gaps
- The record is strong on institutional resilience and weak on any direct Scholz-specific entrenchment behavior, which is itself informative.
- I did not find meaningful evidence that Scholz manipulated elections, courts, media, or term rules in 2022.
- Most negative evidence is about contested committee-chair access or general surveillance/legal disputes, which are procedural and legally checked rather than authoritarian in nature.
- More searching would likely only refine the balance between inherited democratic baseline and Scholz-era institutional maintenance; it is unlikely to uncover a materially different 2022 pattern without a very specific allegation.
